Scenario 3 – DHCP Server Configuration

 Objective
Configure a Server as a DHCP server and assign IP addresses automatically to IoT devices.

Steps Performed
1. Connected the Server to the Home Gateway.
2. Configured the Server IP address.
3. Enabled DHCP Service.
4. Created a DHCP Pool.
5. Configured IoT devices to obtain IP addresses automatically using DHCP.
6. Verified the assigned IP addresses.
7. Tested connectivity using ping.

 Result
The Server successfully assigned IP addresses to the devices through DHCP. The devices received IP addresses automatically and network communication was verified using ping.
